Produce one ConcIR program for the requirements below. The contract is frozen and supplied by the caller; do not modify it.

<domain_requirements>
Model two concurrent tasks named `t1` and `t2` in one module `main` (entry `main::main`). Both tasks acquire the same two mutexes named `a` and `b`, always in the order `a` then `b`: acquire both first, then release them in reverse order. `main` spawns `t1` and `t2` in a `scope`. Use mutex_lock/mutex_unlock and return; do not use rwlock or abstract_step. Program version 3.5.0.
</domain_requirements>

<contract>
{
  "name": "t1-same-order",
  "properties": [
    {
      "kind": "deadlock_free",
      "id": "no-deadlock"
    }
  ],
  "preserved": [
    {
      "kind": "reachable",
      "description": "main::t1 completes",
      "goal": {
        "kind": "function_completed",
        "function": "main::t1"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "reachable",
      "description": "main::t2 completes",
      "goal": {
        "kind": "function_completed",
        "function": "main::t2"
      }
    }
  ],
  "assumptions": {
    "sequential_consistency": true,
    "no_spurious_wakeups": true
  },
  "bounds": {
    "max_threads": 8,
    "max_frames_per_thread": 8,
    "max_states": 20000,
    "max_depth": 64,
    "max_boundary_events": 256
  },
  "allowed_scope": {
    "allow_lock_reorder": true
  }
}
</contract>

Output only the JSON object.

